<title>CANADA: Jordan to redeem Transwest preferreds.</title>
<headline>Jordan to redeem Transwest preferreds.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan Petroleum Ltd said on Thursday that the board of Transwest Energy -- now a wholly owned unit of Jordon -- approved the redemption of its 9.25 percent convertible preferred shares for a total of C$13.6 million.</p>
<p>Jordon said preferred shareholders would receive C$20 per share plus accrued and unpaid dividends.</p>
<p>The company said it expected to mail its notice of redemption on Friday, March 7. The redemption date was set for April 7, it said.</p>
<p>Jordon acquired Transwest last week.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
